title: gdb symbols, types, languages, macros
url:   https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Symbols.html
tags:  gdb debugger symbol type ptype struct language macro cpp

## types
whatis EXPR                       # show the type of an expression, one level  @typeof <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Symbols.html>
whatis struct foo                 # show what a type name is
ptype EXPR                        # show the full type definition of an expression  @struct @definition @fav
ptype TYPE                        # show the full definition of a type
ptype/o struct foo                # show a struct layout with offsets, sizes and padding  @pahole @layout @offsetof
ptype/r TYPE                      # show a type raw, without typedef substitution
ptype/m TYPE                      # show a type without methods
ptype/t TYPE                      # show a type without typedefs
ptype/x struct foo                # show struct offsets in hex, /d for decimal
set opaque-type-resolution on|off # resolve opaque struct types from other files
info vtbl OBJ                     # print the virtual table of a C++ object  @virtual

## symbol lookup
info address SYMBOL             # show where a symbol is stored: register, static, stack
info symbol ADDR                # show which symbol is at an address, e.g. main + 4 in .text  @addr2line @reverse-lookup
info scope LOCATION             # list all variables local to a scope
info types [REGEX]              # list types matching a regex
info types -q REGEX             # list matching types without file headers
info functions [REGEX]          # list functions matching a regex, -q -n -t TYPEREGEX  @list @find
info functions -n ^foo          # list matching functions, skip non-debugging symbols
info variables [REGEX]          # list global and static variables matching a regex  @globals
info variables -q -t int$ REGEX # list variables by name and type regex
info sources [-dirname|-basename] [--] [REGEX] # list all source files  @files
info modules [-q] [REGEX]       # list Fortran modules
info module functions [-m MODREGEX] [-t TYPEREGEX] [REGEX] # list functions in Fortran modules
info module variables [-m MODREGEX] [-t TYPEREGEX] [REGEX] # list variables in Fortran modules
demangle [-l LANG] [--] NAME    # demangle a C++ mangled name  @c++filt
set demangle-style gnu-v3       # choose the demangling style

## symbol internals
maint print symbols [FILE]    # dump full symbols, also maint print psymbols and msymbols
maint info symtabs            # list expanded symbol tables, also maint info psymtabs
maint expand-symtabs [REGEX]  # expand symbol tables now
maint set symbol-cache-size N # set the symbol cache size
maint print symbol-cache      # dump the symbol cache, also symbol-cache-statistics
maint flush symbol-cache      # clear the symbol cache

## languages
show language               # show the current working language  <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Languages.html>
set language auto           # choose the language from the current frame (default)  @local
set language c|c++|d|go|objective-c|opencl|fortran|pascal|rust|modula-2|ada|asm|minimal # set the expression language by hand
info source (language)      # show the language of the current file
set check type on|off       # turn type checking on or off
set check range on|off|warn # turn range checking on or off (Modula-2, Pascal, Ada)
show check type             # show type checking, also show check range

## c and c++
set overload-resolution on|off # resolve C++ overloads in expressions  @cpp <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/C.html>
p OBJ.*MEMFN                   # use a C++ pointer to member  @cpp
p dynamic_cast<D*>(BASE)       # cast in C++ syntax, also static_cast reinterpret_cast const_cast  @cpp
p sizeof(T)                    # get the size of a type or expression
p this->X                      # use "this" in C++ methods  @cpp
set cp-abi auto|gnu-v3         # choose the C++ ABI
show cp-abi                    # show the C++ ABI

## objective-c, rust, go, d
info classes [REGEX]   # list Objective-C classes  @objc
info selectors [REGEX] # list Objective-C selectors  @objc
p [OBJ message]        # send an Objective-C message in an expression  @objc
p X as u32             # cast in Rust syntax  @rust
p X.0                  # get a Rust tuple field  @rust
p MOD::ITEM            # use a Rust path  @rust

## fortran
info common [NAME]                     # show Fortran COMMON blocks  @fortran <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Fortran.html>
set fortran repack-array-slices on|off # repack Fortran array slices  @fortran
p ARR(1:5:2)                           # print a Fortran array slice  @fortran
p SIZE(ARR)                            # call Fortran intrinsics, also LBOUND UBOUND KIND  @fortran

## ada
info tasks                        # list Ada tasks  @ada <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Ada.html>
task N                            # switch to Ada task N  @ada
task apply all CMD                # run CMD on all Ada tasks, also task apply 1 2 -s CMD  @ada
set ada print-signatures on|off   # show signatures of overloaded Ada functions  @ada
set ada trust-PAD-over-XVS on|off # work around old GNAT encodings  @ada
set ada source-charset CHARSET    # set the Ada source character set  @ada

## macros
macro expand EXPR            # show an expression with all macros expanded, needs -g3  @preprocessor @define <https://sourceware.org/gdb/current/onlinedocs/gdb.html/Macros.html>
macro expand-once EXPR       # expand macros only one level
info macro [-a|-all] NAME    # show a macro definition and where it is, -a for all definitions
info macro -- -NAME          # use "--" when the macro name starts with "-"
info macros [LOCATION]       # list all macros visible at a location
macro define NAME(ARGS) BODY # define a macro in GDB
macro define PI 3.14         # define a simple macro in GDB
macro undef NAME             # remove a macro defined in GDB
macro list                   # list macros defined in GDB
p SOME_MACRO(3)              # use a macro in an expression, GDB expands it
